WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.820
Well, of course, if you can imagine what it would be like to develop programming without magnetic tape recorders [laughs].

2
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:28.940
When we wanted to record a concert done by LSU Music School —and they were worth recording—we had to cut them on a disc,

3
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:37.440
by telephone line, from the station to the music building.

4
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.640
Those were recorded on fifteen-inch wax discs.

5
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.413
Platters?

6
00:00:41.413 --> 00:00:42.960
Platters.

7
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:49.580
We tampered with wire recorders for a while but as you know . . .

8
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:49.780
I remember those things.

9
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.160
. . . as you know, [laughs] they were a headache.

10
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.020
It was very difficult to edit.

11
00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:02.740
When you got to the magnetic tape where there was something you didn’t like, you could just cut it out and splice it back together again.

12
00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.240
All of those advantages of magnetic tape, they’re a real boon.

13
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.780
We take it for granted now.

14
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.840
Oh yes.

15
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.240
Audio tape and video tape.

16
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:19.740
But what a great thing it was for broadcasting when magnetic tape came in.

17
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.980
But that was one of our big, big problems.
